1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,775
At U.S. Starbucks, one in ten customers vanished

2
00:00:03,795 --> 00:00:10,227
Jul-Sep 2024, transactions fell 10% from a year earlier

3
00:00:10,247 --> 00:00:14,654
What drove them away was the app Starbucks loved most

4
00:00:14,674 --> 00:00:20,439
One in three U.S. company-store orders comes in by app before arrival

5
00:00:20,459 --> 00:00:24,666
App orders pile on extras like syrup and cold foam

6
00:00:24,686 --> 00:00:29,038
More profit per cup, but each takes longer to make

7
00:00:29,058 --> 00:00:37,088
8 a.m.: the pickup counter fills with app cups; patience cools before the coffee

8
00:00:37,108 --> 00:00:42,501
Founder Howard Schultz called the app Starbucks' biggest Achilles' heel

9
00:00:42,521 --> 00:00:48,002
The CEO at the time was replaced after one year and five months

10
00:00:48,022 --> 00:00:56,249
Starbucks beat a crisis like this in 2008 too. The founder shut about 7,000 U.S. stores at once

11
00:00:56,269 --> 00:00:59,333
For three and a half hours of espresso retraining

12
00:00:59,353 --> 00:01:05,073
Then they fixed the coffee; this time, stores slowed by the app

13
00:01:05,093 --> 00:01:09,595
New CEO Brian Niccol fixed the app instead of dropping it

14
00:01:09,615 --> 00:01:15,987
Menu cut 30%, drinks in 4 minutes: speed added instead of syrup

15
00:01:16,007 --> 00:01:21,437
This year, Apr-Jun 2026, transactions rose 4.2%

16
00:01:21,457 --> 00:01:29,926
In earnings, find the transactions line first. That's where Starbucks fell and recovered

17
00:01:29,946 --> 00:01:36,249
Like and subscribe for more. Full video: profile link
